  "id": "Compound::DB01407 - Gene::153",
  "verbalization": "Clenbuterol exerts its biological effects through binding to Adrb3, a receptor that participates in multiple physiological processes, including Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity and Norepinephrine Binding, as well as Epinephrine Binding. These interactions are mediated through Adrb1, suggesting a complex network of receptor engagement. The evidence indicates that Clenbuterol may influence Adrb1 through its interaction with Adrb3, which in turn modulates receptor activity. The overlapping participation of Adrb3 in different signaling pathways supports the hypothesis that Clenbuterol could act on Adrb1 via a shared receptor or downstream signaling mechanism. The cumulative scores from the paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of Adrb1 involvement remains partially inferred. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Adrb3 as a potential bridge between Clenbuterol and Adrb1, emphasizing the importance of receptor interactions in drug action.",
